# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions.
#
# NOT CURRENTLY IN USE. native-checks.yaml does not pass ubsan-suppressions,
# because doing so breaks the asan half of that workflow: the asan job runs
# inside an R-hub container where the checkout is mounted at /__w/..., while
# the suppressions path is built from `github.workspace`, which is the host's
# /home/runner/work/... . The runtime reports "failed to read suppressions
# file" and the job fails before running anything.
#
# This file is kept, with the entry that would be needed, so that restoring
# the input is a one-line change once the path is resolved inside the
# container. Everything below is what the first instrumented run actually
# reported, not a guess.
#
# One `<check>:<file or function>` per line. Every entry is a deliberate case
# with a reason beside it; anything not named still fails the build.

# AES table generation: `x ^= XTIME(x)` doubles in GF(2^8), and the shift
# promotes to int before truncating back to uint8_t. The truncation is the
# operation, not an accident, and every block cipher is written this way.
#
# Only reachable with the full -fsanitize=integer group. The narrower
# -fsanitize=unsigned-integer-overflow that native-checks.yaml passes does not
# report it, which is why the job is currently green without this file.
implicit-conversion:vendor/tf-psa-crypto/lib/aes.c

# Expected but not yet observed: hash compression functions add modulo 2^32 on
# purpose. If unsigned-integer-overflow starts firing in sha256.c or sha512.c,
# that is why -- and it gets its own line here rather than a wider flag change.
